WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.051
Digital footprints are observable traces created through active sharing, passive collection, public records, technical infrastructure, and third-party references.

00:00:10.051 --> 00:00:17.525
They can be personal, professional, organizational, or technical, and they change over time.

00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:23.453
Active footprints include posts, profiles, documents, and code intentionally published.

00:00:23.453 --> 00:00:30.927
Passive footprints include logs, indexing, metadata, tracking, data-broker records, and reported service exposure.

00:00:30.927 --> 00:00:38.916
One item may be low risk while aggregation reveals sensitive relationships, routines, or infrastructure.

00:00:38.916 --> 00:00:44.328
Responsible analysis validates identity, origin, accuracy, timeliness, and context.

00:00:44.328 --> 00:00:50.772
It distinguishes ownership from association and current conditions from historical records.

00:00:50.772 --> 00:00:58.761
Public availability never authorizes harassment, doxxing, impersonation, unauthorized access, or misuse of personal information.

00:00:58.761 --> 00:01:12.936
Risk reduction combines account security, privacy settings, careful publishing, metadata review, asset ownership, repository and service hygiene, employee awareness, and recurring monitoring for legitimate defensive purposes.

00:01:12.936 --> 00:01:17.833
The objective is intentional control, not total disappearance.

00:01:17.833 --> 00:01:25.822
A well-managed footprint supports useful public communication and accountable operations while limiting unnecessary detail.

00:01:25.822 --> 00:01:36.904
Ethical analysis uses proportionality and evidence to reduce privacy and security risk without exploiting the people represented by the data.
